.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt SSL_CTX_SET_NEW_PENDING_CONN_CB 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm SSL_CTX_set_new_pending_conn_cb ,
.Nm SSL_set_new_pending_conn_cb_fn
.Nd callback function to report creation of QUIC connection SSL objects
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Ft typedef int
.Fo 
.Fa *SSL_set_new_pending_conn_cb_fn
.Fc
(SSL_CTX *c, SSL *new_ssl,
.Bd -literal
                                               void *arg);
 void SSL_CTX_set_new_pending_conn_cb(SSL_CTX *c,
                                     SSL_set_new_pending_conn_cb_fn *f,
                                     void *arg);
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Xr SSL_CTX_set_new_pending_conn_cb 3
sets the new_pending_conn callback function and associated application
data argument
.Em arg .
When using the QUIC transport, TLS handshake processing may occur
independently from the thread which accepts the connection that the
handshake is establishing.
As such,
.Sy SSL
objects representing the connection may be allocated and initialized
prior to a call to
.Xr SSL_accept_connection 3 .
This registered callback may be used to decorate the preallocated
.Sy SSL
object or create other associations with its parent
.Sy SSL
prior to a call to
.Xr SSL_accept_connection 3 .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Xr SSL_CTX_set_new_pending_conn_cb 3
returns no value.
.Pp
SSL_set_new_pending_conn_cb_fn() returns an integer value.
A return value of 0 indicates that the QUIC stack must discard this
newly created
.Sy SSL
object, implying that the associated new connection will not be
available for handling on a subsequent call to
.Xr SSL_accept_connection 3 .
A nonzero return value is treated as success, allowing the new
connection to be enqueued to the accept queue.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr SSL_set_ex_data 3
.Sh NOTES
Callbacks in QUIC connections have some limitations to them that should
be taken into consideration when writing an application.
.Pp
QUIC connections may begin processing prior to when an application calls
.Xr SSL_accept_connection 3
on them.
As such, it may occur that callbacks are delivered to applications'
registered TLS callbacks prior to those SSL objects being returned in
.Xr SSL_accept_connection 3 .
Applications should expect this possibility.
.Pp
In particular no references should be held on SSL objects passed to
callbacks for QUIC connections until such time as they are returned
through a call to SSL_accept_connection.
.El
.Sh HISTORY
.Xr SSL_CTX_set_new_pending_conn_cb 3
was added in OpenSSL 3.5
